rioritized over increasing the reward returns. So any change in the reward critic terms must be less than any change in the cost critic term. If _H_ ∆ is the minimum non-zero difference between any two cost values, and _P_ min is the minimum sampled non-zero likelihood of reaching a particular state and a point in the sample trajectory, then we can bound the maximum change in the reward returns and the maximum change on the weighted cost returns: \n\n\n\n22 \n\n"
